<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kionga Triangle</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kionga Triangle is a small area of land at the mouth of the Rovuma river, on the border between Tanzania and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> took it from Portuguese control in 1894 as part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-east-africa">German East Africa</a>, and Portuguese troops reoccupied it in 1916. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a> of 1919 confirmed it as Portuguese, and it is now part of Mozambique.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kionga-triangle.jpg" alt="Kionga Triangle" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edited by Paul Sprigade (1863-1928), Max Moisel (1869-1920) deriva... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wirtschafts-Atlas_der_deutschen_Kolonien_-_22_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
